Patch 0012 -- id-ordered loop-candidate containers (determinism fix; math unchanged)

Root cause of the run-to-run nondeterministic loop-candidate column in
global_opt_step.tsv on fr1_desk: bow_database::acquire_keyframes() collected
its result in a std::unordered_set<std::shared_ptr<keyframe>> (hashed by
POINTER) and returned a vector copied from it. That vector is consumed in
order by loop_detector::find_continuously_detected_keyframe_sets(), where the
first keyframe whose covisibility set intersects a previous set becomes that
set's lead_keyfrm_ (and marks the previous set "already checked"), so pointer
order (ASLR-dependent) decided the lead candidate and hence which keyframe ids
entered loop_candidates_to_validate_. loop_candidates_to_validate_ itself was
also a pointer-hashed unordered_set, iterated by select_loop_candidate_via_Sim3
and by the step-5 top-n-covisibility expansion.

Changes ONLY container iteration/tie-break order (pointer -> keyframe id, via
the existing nondeterministic:: alias = id_ordered std::set under
-DDETERMINISTIC=ON; identical std::unordered_set otherwise). No arithmetic,
thresholds, or set membership changes:
  * data/bow_database.cc  acquire_keyframes(): final_candidates
  * module/loop_detector.h/.cc  loop_candidates_to_validate_ and the
    select_loop_candidate_via_Sim3() parameter type

